<zk>
	<zscript><![CDATA[
		java.util.Date b = new java.util.Date(126, 3, 1);    // 2026-04-01
		java.util.Date eLong = new java.util.Date(127, 5, 30); // 2027-06-30
		java.util.Date eShort = new java.util.Date(126, 4, 1); // 2026-05-01
		java.util.Date bEdge = new java.util.Date(129, 11, 1);  // 2029-12-01
		java.util.Date eEdge = new java.util.Date(129, 11, 31); // 2029-12-31
		java.util.Date bSpan = new java.util.Date(95, 5, 1);    // 1995-06-01
		java.util.Date eSpan = new java.util.Date(105, 5, 30);  // 2005-06-30
	]]></zscript>
	<label multiline="true">
		Steps to reproduce:
		1. Open each component and switch the calendar from the day view to the month view
			(click the month in the title), then to the year view (click the year).
		2. Compare the selected indication between the datebox and the date range boxes.

		- Expected: the range boxes keep a selected indication. A month or year is selected
			when its own calendar interval intersects the range, so
			2026/04/01~2026/05/01 selects April and May 2026 and the year 2026, and
			2026/04/01~2027/06/30 selects April 2026 through June 2027 and both 2026 and 2027.
			Every panel shows the same range state.
		- Bug: the range boxes show nothing selected in either view — setRangeHighlight is a
			day-view API, and the per-Calendar mark that remains sits on the panel's display
			anchor, which the popup styling suppresses.

		A begin-only range selects just the begin value's month and year, and a hover preview
			in the day view must not turn into a selected month.

		3. Open drbSingle (range 1995/06/01~2005/06/30), drill down to the decade view
			(month title, then year, then decade), and shift a century with `&gt;`, then
			back with `&lt;`.
		- Expected: both centuries paint the 1990s and the 2000s cells — the two decades
			the range covers — whichever arrow brought that century on screen.
		- Bug: after `&gt;` the grid paints nothing. The repaint landed on the outgoing
			grid, which shares its id with the incoming one until the slide ends and is
			then discarded; `&lt;` happens to order the two the other way round.

		4. With a screen reader, walk the month / year / decade grid of drbYearEdge's SECOND
			panel. Its range (2029/12/01~2029/12/31) lies entirely outside the months that
			panel displays.
		- Expected: the panel announces exactly the cells it paints — nothing in the month
			view, 2029 in the year view, 2020-2029 in the decade view. The anchor cell keeps
			the keyboard cursor (aria-activedescendant) without claiming to be selected.
		- Bug: the anchor announces as selected, so the reader hears "January selected"
			while the grid paints the range in a different year.
	</label>
	<datebox id="db" value="${b}"/>
	<daterangebox id="drbLong" numberOfMonths="3" format="yyyy/MM/dd"
		beginValue="${b}" endValue="${eLong}"/>
	<daterangebox id="drbShort" numberOfMonths="2" format="yyyy/MM/dd"
		beginValue="${b}" endValue="${eShort}"/>
	<daterangebox id="drbBeginOnly" numberOfMonths="2" format="yyyy/MM/dd"
		beginValue="${b}"/>
	<!-- One panel, so it is both the leftmost and the rightmost: linked panels hide
		the inner-edge arrow, and this is the shape where a single panel can be
		shifted BOTH ways. Its range straddles 1999/2000, so BOTH centuries the
		decade view can reach (the calendar clamps to 1900..2099) paint the same two
		decades — whichever arrow brought that century on screen. -->
	<daterangebox id="drbSingle" numberOfMonths="1" format="yyyy/MM/dd"
		beginValue="${bSpan}" endValue="${eSpan}"/>
	<!-- A range pinned to the last month of a decade: panel 1 is anchored to
		2030/01, so its month grid holds none of the range, its year grid holds the
		range's year but not its own anchor year, and its decade grid holds the
		range's decade but not its own. The one shape where a panel's anchor is
		outside the painted range in all three views. -->
	<daterangebox id="drbYearEdge" numberOfMonths="2" format="yyyy/MM/dd"
		beginValue="${bEdge}" endValue="${eEdge}"/>

	<label multiline="true">
		5. Click "push Almaty instant", open drbAlmaty and switch to the month view.
			1709231400000 is 2024-02-29T18:30:00Z, which Asia/Almaty reads as Feb 29 23:30
			— within half an hour of the offset change that ends February there.
		- Expected: Feb 29 is the selected DAY and February the selected month — the day
			and the month the range's begin instant falls in.
		- Bug: nothing selected in the day view and March in the month view. Both passes
			matched by building each month's epoch bounds from wall-clock midnight, and
			February's upper bound landed on the pre-change offset — an hour BEFORE the
			instant it was supposed to contain, while March's lower bound landed before
			it. In the day view that dropped the panel from the overlap test, so its
			whole highlight was cleared rather than merely shifted a day.
		6. Same with "push Cairo instant": 1730410200000 is 2024-10-31T21:30:00Z, which
			Africa/Cairo reads as Oct 31 23:30, in the hour DST end makes ambiguous.
		- Expected: Oct 31 and October.
		- Bug: neither — both October's upper bound and November's lower bound fell on
			the far side of the instant.

		Only a server-pushed instant reaches this: a pick in the popup is box-tz
			midnight, which never lands within an hour of a month boundary.
	</label>
	<button id="btnAlmaty" label="push Almaty instant"
		onClick='drbAlmaty.setBeginValue(new java.util.Date(1709231400000L))'/>
	<daterangebox id="drbAlmaty" numberOfMonths="1" format="yyyy/MM/dd"
		timeZone="Asia/Almaty"/>
	<button id="btnCairo" label="push Cairo instant"
		onClick='drbCairo.setBeginValue(new java.util.Date(1730410200000L))'/>
	<daterangebox id="drbCairo" numberOfMonths="1" format="yyyy/MM/dd"
		timeZone="Africa/Cairo"/>
</zk>
